READING
======================================================================================================================
  H1 FAILS: 0/16 cases lie within 10% of the target over x in [0.1, 30].
  Point mass: C_V/C_T = (1 + x)/x = 11.000, 2.000, 1.3333, 1.1000, 1.0333 at x = 0.1, 1, 3, 10, 30; within 10% only on [10.000, 30.000].
  Why: Verlinde's M_D = M x at every radius (an r^-2 dark density all the way in; g = g_N + sqrt(a_V g_N), a linear sum), while the
  target's cold mass is M (sqrt(1 + x^2) - 1) (an r^-1 density inside r_M; g = sqrt(g_N^2 + a0 g_N)).  They share only the deep limit,
  approached as 1/x.  The density ratio sqrt(1 + x^2)/x carries the small-x failure; the field ratio (1 + x)/sqrt(1 + x^2) (max sqrt 2 at x = 1)
  carries the large-x tail.
  Normalisation: kappa_V = 0.482 (H_Lambda) and 0.583 (H0) both lie within 2 sigma of both fitted windows.
  G2 UNDEFINED, G3 UNDEFINED, G4 PASS (count only), G5 FAIL (Solar System, Hees et al. 2017).  A scoped no-go on G1.

  kappa = 1/2 and Omega_c h^2 stay FITTED.  Nothing here says the data favour either model, or that the theory is closed.

